55,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Now we have the options. Option A is very flexible, but I worry we might lose that closeness if we are always moving.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option A is a disaster for fairness; the early arrivals get the best seats. Option B is stable, but we must be honest about the assignments.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,Option A and C sound expensive because of the power re-runs. Option B seems the safest for the budget.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Mio,,Option A sounds like a lot of work every morning! I don't want to spend ten minutes just plugging in my screens!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option A and C are absurd. You cannot calibrate a workstation if you move every day or every few months. Option B is the only choice.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Toshio, if we choose Option B, can we make sure the seating helps us communicate better, as the new joiners liked?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"Yes, as long as we explicitly decide who sits where, including the interior wall seats, to avoid the habits of the past.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I agree with Option B. It's the only one that doesn't risk repeated facilities charges.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Mio,,I'm with you! Option B means we have a home base. No more morning scramble! I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Finally, some sense. Option B provides the physical stability required for actual work. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"If everyone feels it is the most stable and fair, I am happy. I will vote for Option B to keep our harmony.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Toshio,,It is the only logical choice that addresses both the financial constraints and the need for a fair distribution of space. I vote B.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I feel comfortable with this. It's the most cautious approach. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Mio,,Yay! We all agree! Let's make our fixed spots super cozy!,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"It's a relief we aren't choosing a ""rotating"" nightmare. I've already cast my vote for B.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
